  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract activity in Oklahoma through FY2026 to date shows concentrated buying and large awards. The state received $4.6B in contract obligations across 19,346 awards, with an average award size of $237K. Obligations fell 32.6% year over year in the current fiscal year to date. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, while Aircraft Manufacturing, Engineering Services, and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing are the top industry recipients. THE BOEING COMPANY, twice listed among top vendors, and several defense and IT contractors capture the largest shares of obligations. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity. Practitioners tracking opportunities should note the mix of large prime awards alongside many smaller transactions given the award count and average award size.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying the most federal contracts in Oklahoma?",
        "body": "Department of Defense obligated $3B, making it the top buyer in Oklahoma for FY2026 to date. Department of Transportation obligated $634M and Department of Health and Human Services obligated $218M. General Services Administration obligated $212M, and Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $171M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate federal spending in Oklahoma?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing received $836M, the largest industry share in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services received $410M, Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing received $368M, and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation received $340M. THE BOEING COMPANY is the largest vendor at $980M, followed by a second listing of THE BOEING COMPANY at $179M and V2X AEROSPACE LLC at $119M."
      }
    ]
  },
